1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Let me show you something real quick.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:06,600
This is a board our parish
runs on the internet.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:14,000
It works like the corkboard in the front of the
church, except it can let you know when someone answers.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,800
Need a hand? Lend one.

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,600
That's the whole idea.

6
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:23,800
Neighbors ask, neighbors answer, and a real
person you know makes the introduction.

7
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:27,800
You get in with a code from your parish.

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,200
No app store, no credit card.

9
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,400
If you have the code, you're already welcome.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
When you sign in, the parish greets you by
name, with a line the coordinators wrote.

11
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,600
One ask that could use a hand today,
and the pulse of the week underneath.

12
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:47,600
A crib found a home.

13
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,400
A neighbor stepped up.

14
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,600
Nobody's name gets paraded.

15
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,600
Asking takes about a minute.

16
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,200
Pick a category, say it in a line or two.

17
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,600
A ride to Mass, math help for your
kid, a hand with the groceries.

18
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:08,200
And the promise is printed right on your ask: nothing
about you is shared until you accept a match.

19
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,600
Everything lives on one board,
asks and offers side by side.

20
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:14,800
A ride to the 9:30 Mass.

21
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:16,800
Two extra dinners most weeks.

22
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:19,400
A retired teacher, patience included.

23
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,400
When somebody can help, a
coordinator proposes the match.

24
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:26,600
A person who knows you both, not an algorithm.

25
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:30,400
Both sides get a plain yes or no,
and nothing is revealed yet.

26
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,600
And when both say yes, there it is.

27
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,400
Contact, shared between the two of you alone.

28
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:40,800
The page says it better than I can: reach out
kindly and arrange the rest together.

29
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,800
From here it's two neighbors and a phone call.

30
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,600
Now, everything you just watched
is our demo parish.

31
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,600
St. Brigid's isn't real, and
every name here is invented.

32
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:54,400
But the software is real, it's open,
and any parish can run its own.

33
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:58,000
If that sounds like yours, come read
at reciprocal aid dot network.

34
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Ready to begin? Ask your
coordinator for a code.
